 "about": "Crowning cartouche of the Garden Gate (plate 4, 'North Side of Garden Gate'), left half, traced on the Palace Museum copy (album_2.jpg, public domain) in its own pixels: the cap with its coronet, the palmette, the outer frame with its feet and the inner C-scrolls. Bands are raised straps of the given width along a Catmull-Rom centre line; closed shapes are raised forms; ground_at marks the hatched (sunk) fields. The right half is the mirror image about x 2482, the attic's axis (both halves of the frame fit best about 2482, the cap about 2482.5). The eave polyline runs about 5 px under the attic eave's top, from the axis into the frame's foot, and closes the crown's body against it (the feet stand outside it).",
